cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Testing the Thermal-Horizon Reading of the Radial Acceleration Relation, from Galaxies to Wide Binaries"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hájek"
    given-names: "Filip"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheCake/thermal-horizon-rar"
abstract: >-
  Measurement and theory-testing program for gravity at low accelerations:
  coefficient-level tests of the radial acceleration relation on SPARC and
  KiDS-1000 lensing data; a joint two-dimensional (velocity, direction-angle)
  likelihood measurement of the low-acceleration velocity boost in 14,071 Gaia
  EDR3 wide binaries with full seed and bootstrap error budgets; the solar-system
  quadrupole consequences of the measured boost; a modified-inertia versus
  modified-gravity discrimination on the binary data; and a reconciliation by
  ablation of the conflicting published wide-binary analyses. The manuscript is
  PAPER.md; the chronological lab notebook (including all corrections and
  retractions) is NOTES-horizon-inertia.md; every claimed number is reproduced
  by a named script under calcs/.
keywords:
  - MOND
  - radial acceleration relation
  - wide binaries
  - Gaia
  - modified gravity
  - modified inertia
  - external field effect
  - galactic dynamics
